---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import VideoPlaceholder from '../components/VideoPlaceholder.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <div class="about">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

    <VideoPlaceholder />

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2 class="about-section__heading">How I got here</h2>
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>
          For as long as I can remember, I've loved to draw. I never had any
          real formal training, but it came to me naturally and I spent all
          my spare time with a pencil in hand. When it came time to figure out
          what I wanted to be when I "grew up," I had little to no support in
          taking the path of a professional artist. So I went looking for
          something adjacent, and found graphic design almost by accident.
          Turned out it was something I'd already been doing without a name
          for it.
        </p>
        <p>
          I went on to study Communication Design at Texas State University,
          expecting to end up somewhere in traditional graphic design,
          branding, or advertising worlds. Then the iPhone came out, and the
          whole direction of design shifted. I dove headfirst into the web
          and product side of the industry instead, and never looked back.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2 class="about-section__heading">What keeps me here</h2>
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>
          Product design, at its core, is about making sense of ambiguity.
          That's not a side effect of the job. It is the job. Most of what I
          enjoy is playing detective: taking an unclear problem and finding
          the path through it. Mix that with a love of aesthetics and
          craftsmanship, and you have what I love most about this industry.
        </p>
        <p>
          The other piece is people. Some of the best parts of this career
          have come from being in rooms with people smarter than me and
          learning from them. That's stayed true across every team I've been
          on. The many talented, intelligent, and interesting individuals have
          helped me grow in both a professional and personal capacity. I'm
          forever grateful for this.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2 class="about-section__heading">Outside of work</h2>
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>
          I'm a husband and father first, and that's where most of my time
          and attention goes these days. Staying active and healthy matters to
          me, and I try to keep that a consistent part of life, not an
          afterthought. And even though most of my creative energy goes into
          the work itself these days, I try to draw and paint when I can
          (even if it's just crayons and finger paint with the kiddos).
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .about-section + .about-section {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .about-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .about-section__heading {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    line-height: var(--line-height-tight);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .about-prose p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-regular);
    line-height: var(--line-height-loose);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .about-prose p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>
